<template>
  <article class="doc-page">
    <div class="doc-breadcrumb"><span>02</span><i></i><span>Backend introduction</span></div>
    <header class="doc-hero"><h1>Meet the<br><em>server boundary.</em></h1><p>Move from a browser component to a trustworthy application: handler-only SFC routes, connected services, validation, persistence, and the security rules that keep client authority where it belongs.</p><div class="doc-meta"><span>Intermediate</span><span>~30 minutes</span><span>Data adapters</span><span>SQLite</span></div></header>
    <nav class="doc-toc"><b>ON THIS PAGE</b><a href="#boundary">Trust boundary</a><a href="#handlers">Handlers</a><a href="#adapters">Adapters</a><a href="#data">Data</a><a href="#realtime">Pub/sub</a><a href="#production">Production</a></nav>

    <section class="doc-section" id="boundary"><div class="doc-section-head"><span>02.1</span><div><h2>The browser asks. The server decides.</h2><p class="doc-lead">Route guards improve UX; they do not authorize data. Every mutation must be validated again at the HTTP boundary.</p></div></div>
      <div class="doc-flow"><div><b>SFC component</b><span>UNTRUSTED REQUEST</span></div><i>→</i><div><b>HTTP handler</b><span>PARSE + VALIDATE</span></div><i>→</i><div><b>Domain operation</b><span>AUTHORIZE</span></div><i>→</i><div><b>SQLite</b><span>ATOMIC COMMIT</span></div></div>
      <div class="doc-grid three"><div class="doc-card"><span>PARSE</span><h3>Bound the input</h3><p>Limit body size, require JSON, normalize strings, and reject malformed keys.</p></div><div class="doc-card"><span>AUTHORIZE</span><h3>Derive identity</h3><p>Use server sessions—not IDs supplied in a request body—to determine ownership.</p></div><div class="doc-card"><span>RESPOND</span><h3>Minimize output</h3><p>Return stable error shapes and never expose stack traces or private rows.</p></div></div>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section" id="handlers"><div class="doc-section-head"><span>02.2</span><div><h2>Handler-only SFC routes</h2><p class="doc-lead">An SFC can declare an HTTP route without shipping a browser component. The compiler emits a client-safe no-op, keeping server dependencies out of the bundle.</p></div></div>
      <div class="doc-code"><div class="doc-code-head"><span>api/Feedback.sfc</span><b>SERVER ONLY</b></div><pre><code data-snippet="handler"></code></pre></div>
      <aside class="doc-note"><b>BUNDLE SAFETY</b><p>No template and no component tag means handler-only. Imports such as <code class="doc-inline">better-sqlite3</code> stay on the server side instead of leaking into client chunks.</p></aside>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section" id="adapters"><div class="doc-section-head"><span>02.3</span><div><h2>Connect capabilities, not credentials</h2><p class="doc-lead">A data adapter is a server-only capability. Components call named operations; configuration owns the remote address, authentication, and transport.</p></div></div>
      <div class="doc-flow"><div><b>Named operation</b><span>VALIDATED INPUT</span></div><i>â†’</i><div><b>Authorization</b><span>SERVER IDENTITY</span></div><i>â†’</i><div><b>Data adapter</b><span>OPAQUE SECRET</span></div><i>â†’</i><div><b>Remote service</b><span>HTTP OR SSH</span></div></div>
      <div class="doc-code"><div class="doc-code-head"><span>sfc.data.js</span><b>SERVER CONFIGURATION</b></div><pre><code data-snippet="adapters"></code></pre></div>
      <div class="doc-code"><div class="doc-code-head"><span>api/Deployments.sfc</span><b>ALLOWLISTED OPERATION</b></div><pre><code data-snippet="adapterHandler"></code></pre></div>
      <table class="doc-table"><thead><tr><th>AXIS</th><th>BUILT IN</th><th>RULE</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Secrets</td><td>Environment and files</td><td>Resolve on the server; redact when serialized</td></tr><tr><td>HTTP auth</td><td>Bearer, basic, API key, OAuth2, mTLS</td><td>Never accept credentials or target URLs from the browser</td></tr><tr><td>Transport</td><td>Direct HTTP/TLS and OpenSSH tunnels</td><td>Verify host keys and bind forwarded ports to loopback</td></tr></tbody></table>
      <aside class="doc-note blue"><b>FAIL CLOSED</b><p>Every named operation requires input validation and either an authorization function or an explicit <code class="doc-inline">public: true</code>. Missing environment secrets stop the request instead of becoming empty credentials.</p></aside>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section" id="data"><div class="doc-section-head"><span>02.4</span><div><h2>Separate transport from storage</h2><p class="doc-lead">Keep request/response mechanics in the API layer and prepared database operations in a data module.</p></div></div>
      <table class="doc-table"><thead><tr><th>LAYER</th><th>OWNS</th><th>NEVER OWNS</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Component</td><td>Loading, errors, rendering</td><td>Authorization decisions</td></tr><tr><td>API handler</td><td>Origin, session, schema validation</td><td>Raw HTML rendering</td></tr><tr><td>Database module</td><td>Transactions and prepared statements</td><td>HTTP response details</td></tr></tbody></table>
      <div class="doc-code"><div class="doc-code-head"><span>notes-db.js</span><b>PREPARED + ATOMIC</b></div><pre><code data-snippet="database"></code></pre></div>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section" id="realtime"><div class="doc-section-head"><span>02.5</span><div><h2>Realtime is still a database write</h2><p class="doc-lead">The integrated pub/sub endpoint validates JSON, commits a monotonic version in SQLite WAL mode, then fans the event out over a multiplexed SSE connection.</p></div></div>
      <div class="doc-flow"><div><b>PUT value</b><span>SAME-ORIGIN CHECK</span></div><i>→</i><div><b>CAS transaction</b><span>VERSION N + 1</span></div><i>→</i><div><b>Event log</b><span>CROSS-PROCESS</span></div><i>→</i><div><b>SSE topics</b><span>BOUNDED QUEUES</span></div></div>
      <div class="doc-code"><div class="doc-code-head"><span>optimistic update</span><b>NO LOST INCREMENTS</b></div><pre><code data-snippet="cas"></code></pre></div>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section" id="production"><div class="doc-section-head"><span>02.6</span><div><h2>Development convenience, production refusal</h2><p class="doc-lead">The server loads increasingly specific local environment files, but already-injected process variables always win. Production still fails closed when its HTTPS identity is missing.</p></div></div>
      <div class="doc-code"><div class="doc-code-head"><span>terminal</span><b>MODES</b></div><pre><code data-snippet="commands"></code></pre></div>
    </section>
    <a class="doc-next" href="/advanced"><span>NEXT CHAPTER<strong>Full-stack SFC patterns</strong></span><i>→</i></a>
  </article>
</template>
<script lang="ts">
const snippets = {
  handler: `<script>\nimport { feedbackDb } from '../../feedback-db.js';\n\nexport default {\n  async postHandler(body, req, res) {\n    const message = validateMessage(body.message);\n    if (!message) return json(res, 400, { error: 'Invalid message' });\n    const row = feedbackDb.create({ message, now: Date.now() });\n    return json(res, 201, { feedback: row });\n  }\n};\n<\/script>\n\n<${'route'} path="/api/feedback" methods="POST" />`,
  adapters: `import {\n  bearerAuth, createDataLayer, createSshTunnel,\n  defineAdapters, defineOperations, env, httpAdapter\n} from './data-adapters.js';\n\nconst deploymentApi = httpAdapter({\n  baseUrl: process.env.DEPLOY_API_URL,\n  auth: bearerAuth(env('DEPLOY_API_TOKEN'))\n});\n\nconst privateApi = httpAdapter({\n  baseUrl: 'http://inventory.internal:8080/',\n  transport: createSshTunnel({\n    host: 'production-bastion', // ~/.ssh/config alias\n    targetHost: 'inventory.internal', targetPort: 8080\n  })\n});\n\nexport const data = createDataLayer({\n  adapters: defineAdapters({ deploymentApi, privateApi }),\n  operations: defineOperations({\n    listDeployments: {\n      adapter: 'deploymentApi',\n      validate: input => typeof input?.service === 'string' && input.service.length < 80\n        ? { service: input.service } : false,\n      authorize: context => context.session?.role === 'operator',\n      run: (api, input) => api.request(\`deployments?service=\${encodeURIComponent(input.service)}\`)\n    }\n  })\n});`,
  adapterHandler: `<script>\nimport { data } from '../../sfc.data.js';\n\nexport default {\n  async postHandler(body, req, res) {\n    const session = await requireSession(req);\n    const result = await data.execute(\n      'listDeployments', body, { session }\n    );\n    return json(res, 200, result.data);\n  }\n};\n<\/script>\n\n<${'route'} path="/api/deployments" methods="POST" />`,
  database: `const insert = db.prepare(\`\n  INSERT INTO notes (id, owner_id, body, created_at)\n  VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)\n\`);\n\nexport function createNote(session, body) {\n  // owner_id comes from the authenticated server session.\n  const note = { id: randomUUID(), ownerId: session.user_id, body };\n  insert.run(note.id, note.ownerId, note.body, Date.now());\n  return note;\n}`,
  cas: `const counter = realtimeValue('room/counter', 0);\n\n// Reads the current version, attempts a compare-and-set,\n// and retries cleanly if another client wins first.\nawait counter.update(current => current + 1);`,
  commands: `# Copy the safe template; .env files are gitignored\nCopy-Item .env.example .env.local\n\n# Fast JIT development; loads .env* automatically\nnpm run serve:dev\n\n# Built output on loopback, no production identity required\nnpm run build\nnpm run serve:preview\n\n# Real production: injected variables override files\n$env:AUTH_ORIGIN='https://app.example.com'\n$env:AUTH_RP_ID='app.example.com'\nnpm run serve`
};
export default class extends HTMLElement { static tag='sfc-intermediate-page'; connectedCallback(){ this.querySelectorAll('[data-snippet]').forEach(n=>n.textContent=snippets[n.getAttribute('data-snippet')]); } }
</script>
<route path="/intermediate" methods="GET" />
